# SwiftPM build directories.
#
# The wildcard matters. A plain `.build/` matches only a directory named exactly
# `.build`, so the alternate scratch paths this repository's scripts use —
# `.build-uni/` and `.build-universal/` — slipped through and would have been
# committed. Together they are over 500 MB of compiler output.
.build*/

# Packaging output: CodexBridger.app, the .dmg and the .zip.
build/

# Xcode state, for anyone who opens the package in Xcode rather than the CLI.
*.xcodeproj
*.xcworkspace
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/
.swiftpm/

# Design notes, field reference, test report, generated samples and screenshots.
# These stay local: they are working material for whoever develops the app, not part of
# what a user needs to build or run it. Nothing the README links to lives here.
docs/

# Codex creates a scratch directory inside any CODEX_HOME it reads.
tmp/

# Credentials. This app handles API keys, so a stray .env or key file in the
# working tree is a realistic accident rather than a hypothetical one.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

# Editor and OS files.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
